<resources>
    <!--
      How much of the screen a floating panel may take, as a percentage of its height.

      This is the whole card, not the list inside it. Capping the list says nothing about how
      tall the panel ends up, because the header, the hairlines and three action rows are added
      on top of it, and a list allowed most of a landscape screen produced a card that ran off
      the top of it and covered the controls it was opened from.

      Upright there is height to spare and the panel should not take it. On a phone lying down
      the whole screen is about as tall as a portrait panel, so the share has to be larger even
      though the result is smaller: a strict cap there means controls that exist in one
      orientation and not the other, which is exactly the complaint this answers.
    -->
    <integer name="sheet_max_height_percent">76</integer>
</resources>
